Hi Yeikel,=20
=20
Neat question! And thanks for the link to the RestClient code; very helpful=
.=20
=20
I don't believe there's a way to configure Kafka Connect to add these=20
headers to forwarded requests right now. You may be able to do some kind of=
=20
out-of-band proxy magic to intercept forwarded requests and insert the=20
proper headers there.=20
=20
I don't see a reason for Kafka Connect to only forward authorization=20
headers, even after examining the PR [1] and corresponding Jira ticket [2]=
=20
that altered the RestClient class to begin including authorization headers=
=20
in forwarded REST requests. We may be able to tweak the RestClient to=20
include all headers instead of just the authorization header. I know that=
=20
this doesn't help your immediate situation, but if other committers and=20
contributors agree that the change would be beneficial, we may be able to=
=20
include it in the next release (which may be 3.7.0, or a patch release for=
=20
3.4, 3.5, or 3.6). Alternatively, we may have to gate such a change behind=
=20
a feature flag (either a coarse-grained boolean that enables/disables=20
forwarding of all non-authorization headers, or more fine-grained logic=20
such as include/exclude lists or even regexes), which would require a KIP=
=20
and may take longer to release.=20
=20
I've CC'd the dev list to gather their perspective on this potential=20
change, and to solicit their input on possible workarounds that may be=20
useful to you sooner than the next release takes place.=20
=20
[1] - https://github.com/apache/kafka/pull/6791=20
[2] - https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-8404=20
=20
Cheers,=20
=20
Chris=20
