Hello,

KAFKA-15571 [1] was merged and backported to the 3.5 and 3.6 branches. =
Bug fixes the feature that was added in 3.5. Considering the feature =
doesn't work as expected without a fix, I would like to know if it's =
reasonable to start the 3.5.2 release. Of course, releasing such a =
massive project like Kafka is not a trivial task, and I am looking for =
the community's input on this if it's reasonable to start the 3.5.2 =
release process.

Best,
Levani

[1] - https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-15571=

