David Jacot created KAFKA-15603:
-----------------------------------

             Summary: kafka-dump-log --offsets-decoder should handle parsin=
g errors
                 Key: KAFKA-15603
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-15603
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
            Reporter: David Jacot


I needed to dump an __consumer_offset partition so I used `kafka-dump-log -=
-offsets-decoder --files <path>` to do it but I got the following error:

=C2=A0
Exception in thread "main" org.apache.kafka.common.protocol.types.SchemaExc=
eption: Buffer underflow while parsing consumer protocol's header
=09at org.apache.kafka.clients.consumer.internals.ConsumerProtocol.deserial=
izeVersion(ConsumerProtocol.java:72)
=09at org.apache.kafka.clients.consumer.internals.ConsumerProtocol.deserial=
izeAssignment(ConsumerProtocol.java:179)
=09at kafka.coordinator.group.GroupMetadataManager$.$anonfun$parseGroupMeta=
data$2(GroupMetadataManager.scala:1562)
=09at kafka.coordinator.group.GroupMetadataManager$.parseGroupMetadata(Grou=
pMetadataManager.scala:1560)
=09at kafka.coordinator.group.GroupMetadataManager$.formatRecordKeyAndValue=
(GroupMetadataManager.scala:1526)
=09at kafka.tools.DumpLogSegments$OffsetsMessageParser.parse(DumpLogSegment=
s.scala:416)
=09at kafka.tools.DumpLogSegments$.$anonfun$dumpLog$2(DumpLogSegments.scala=
:327)
=09at kafka.tools.DumpLogSegments$.$anonfun$dumpLog$2$adapted(DumpLogSegmen=
ts.scala:285)
=09at scala.collection.IterableOnceOps.foreach(IterableOnce.scala:575)
=09at scala.collection.IterableOnceOps.foreach$(IterableOnce.scala:573)
=09at scala.collection.AbstractIterable.foreach(Iterable.scala:933)
=09at kafka.tools.DumpLogSegments$.$anonfun$dumpLog$1(DumpLogSegments.scala=
:285)
=09at kafka.tools.DumpLogSegments$.$anonfun$dumpLog$1$adapted(DumpLogSegmen=
ts.scala:282)
=09at scala.collection.IterableOnceOps.foreach(IterableOnce.scala:575)
=09at scala.collection.IterableOnceOps.foreach$(IterableOnce.scala:573)
=09at scala.collection.AbstractIterable.foreach(Iterable.scala:933)
=09at kafka.tools.DumpLogSegments$.dumpLog(DumpLogSegments.scala:282)
=09at kafka.tools.DumpLogSegments$.$anonfun$main$1(DumpLogSegments.scala:70=
)
=09at kafka.tools.DumpLogSegments$.main(DumpLogSegments.scala:61)
=09at kafka.tools.DumpLogSegments.main(DumpLogSegments.scala)
Caused by: java.nio.BufferUnderflowException
=09at java.base/java.nio.Buffer.nextGetIndex(Buffer.java:707)
=09at java.base/java.nio.HeapByteBuffer.getShort(HeapByteBuffer.java:383)
