Thanks for the KIP Hanyu,

One questions:

> To address this inconsistency, we propose that KeyQuery  should be restricted to querying kv-stores  only, ensuring that it always returns a plain V  type, making the behavior of the aforementioned code more predictable. Similarly, RangeQuery  should be dedicated to querying kv-stores , consistently returning only the plain V .

Why do you want to restrict `KeyQuery` and `RangeQuery` to kv-stores? I 
think it would be possible to still allow both queries for ts-kv-stores, 
but change the implementation to return "plain V" instead of 
`ValueAndTimestamp<V>`, ie, the implementation would automatically 
unwrap the value.



-Matthias

