> INVALID_TXN_STATE is being returned even though the partitions have been added to the transaction (AddPartitionsToTxn). Nothing about the code has changed between 3.5 and 3.6, and I have loop-integration-tested this code against 3.5 thousands of times. 3.6 is newly - and always - returning INVALID_TXN_STATE. If I change the code to retry on INVALID_TXN_STATE, I eventually quickly (always) receive UNKNOWN_SERVER_ERROR. In looking at the broker logs, the broker indicates that sequence numbers are out of order - but (a) I am repeating requests that were in order (so something on the broker got a little haywire maybe? or maybe this is due to me ignoring invalid_txn_state?), _and_ I am not receiving OUT_OF_ORDER_SEQUENCE_NUMBER, I am receiving UNKNOWN_SERVER_ERROR.
> I think the main problem is the client unexpectedly receiving INVALID_TXN_STATE, but a second problem here is that OOOSN is being mapped to USE on return for some reason.



