Subject: [jira] [Created] (KAFKA-15755) LeaveGroupResponse v0-v2 should
 handle no members
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable
X-JIRA-FingerPrint: 30527f35849b9dde25b450d4833f0394

Robert Wagner created KAFKA-15755:
-------------------------------------

             Summary: LeaveGroupResponse v0-v2 should handle no members
                 Key: KAFKA-15755
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-15755
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
            Reporter: Robert Wagner


When Sarama and Librdkafka consumer clients issue LeaveGroup requests, they=
 use an older protocol version < 3 which did not include a `members` field.

Since our upgrade the kafka broker 3.4.1 we have started seeing these broke=
r exceptions:

{code}
[2023-10-24 01:17:17,214] ERROR [KafkaApi-28598] Unexpected error handling =
request RequestHeader(apiKey=3DLEAVE_GROUP, apiVersion=3D1, clientId=3DREDA=
CTED, correlationId=3D116775, headerVersion=3D1) -- LeaveGroupRequestData(g=
roupId=3DREDACTED, memberId=3D'REDACTED-73967453-93c4-4f3f-bcef-32c1f280350=
f', members=3D[]) with context RequestContext(header=3DRequestHeader(apiKey=
=3DLEAVE_GROUP, apiVersion=3D1, clientId=3DREDACTED, correlationId=3D116775=
, headerVersion=3D1), connectionId=3D'REDACTED', clientAddress=3D/REDACTED,=
 principal=3DREDACTED, listenerName=3DListenerName(PLAINTEXT), securityProt=
ocol=3DPLAINTEXT, clientInformation=3DClientInformation(softwareName=3Dconf=
luent-kafka-python, softwareVersion=3D1.7.0-rdkafka-1.7.0), fromPrivilegedL=
istener=3Dfalse, principalSerde=3DOptional[REDACTED]) (kafka.server.KafkaAp=
is)
java.util.concurrent.CompletionException: org.apache.kafka.common.errors.Un=
supportedVersionException: LeaveGroup response version 1 can only contain o=
ne member, got 0 members.
=09at java.base/java.util.concurrent.CompletableFuture.encodeThrowable(Comp=
letableFuture.java:315)
=09at java.base/java.util.concurrent.CompletableFuture.completeThrowable(Co=
mpletableFuture.java:320)
=09at java.base/java.util.concurrent.CompletableFuture.uniHandle(Completabl=
eFuture.java:936)
=09at java.base/java.util.concurrent.CompletableFuture.uniHandleStage(Compl=
etableFuture.java:950)
=09at java.base/java.util.concurrent.CompletableFuture.handle(CompletableFu=
ture.java:2340)
=09at kafka.server.KafkaApis.handleLeaveGroupRequest(KafkaApis.scala:1796)
=09at kafka.server.KafkaApis.handle(KafkaApis.scala:196)
=09at kafka.server.KafkaRequestHandler.run(KafkaRequestHandler.scala:75)
=09at java.base/java.lang.Thread.run(Thread.java:833)
Caused by: org.apache.kafka.common.errors.UnsupportedVersionException: Leav=
eGroup response version 1 can only contain one member, got 0 members. {code=
}
=C2=A0
KIP-848 introduced a check in LeaveGroupResponse that the members field mus=
t have 1 element.  In some error cases, it seems like the members field has=
 0 elements - which would still be a valid response for v0-v2 messages, but=
 this exception was being thrown.

Instead of throwing an exception in this case, continue with the LeaveGroup=
Response, since it is not a field included in v0 - v2 responses anyway.



