Subject: [jira] [Created] (KAFKA-15768)
 StateQueryResult#getOnlyPartitionResult should not throw for
 FailedQueryResult
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable
X-JIRA-FingerPrint: 30527f35849b9dde25b450d4833f0394

Matthias J. Sax created KAFKA-15768:
---------------------------------------

             Summary: StateQueryResult#getOnlyPartitionResult should not th=
row for FailedQueryResult
                 Key: KAFKA-15768
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-15768
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
          Components: streams
            Reporter: Matthias J. Sax


Calling `StateQueryResult#getOnlyPartitionResult` crashes with an incorrect=
 `IllegalArgumentException` if the only result is a `FailedQueryResult`.

The issue is the internal `filter(r -> r.getResult() !=3D 0)` step, that bl=
indly (and incorrectly) calls `getResult`.

Given the semantics of `getOnlyPartitionResult` we should not care if the r=
esult is SuccessQueryResult or FailedQueryResult, but only check if there i=
s a single result or not. (The user has not means to avoid getting an excep=
tion otherwise.)

Side-note: why does `FailedQueryResult#getResult` throw an IllegalArgumentE=
xception (there is no argument passed into the method =E2=80=93 it should r=
ather be an `IllegalStateException` =E2=80=93 but I guess we would need a K=
IP for this fix?)



--
